Teach openal-soft that visionOS is a device platform, not desktop macOS.

Two guards miss visionOS, both because they test TARGET_OS_IOS /
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME against an explicit list. On visionOS TARGET_OS_IPHONE is 1
but TARGET_OS_IOS is 0, and CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is visionOS, so both fall
through to the macOS branch:

  1. coreaudio.cpp includes <IOKit/audio/IOAudioTypes.h> for device
     enumeration. XROS.sdk has no such header -- enumeration is macOS-only
     here, exactly as on iOS and tvOS.
  2. CMakeLists.txt links -framework AudioUnit -framework ApplicationServices.
     Neither is linkable on visionOS; AudioUnit is subsumed by AudioToolbox
     and ApplicationServices does not exist.

Upstreamable as-is.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 060a740..c02c9b7 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1130,7 +1130,7 @@ if(ALSOFT_BACKEND_COREAUDIO)
         set(BACKENDS  "${BACKENDS} CoreAudio,")
 
         set(EXTRA_LIBS -Wl,-framework,CoreAudio ${EXTRA_LIBS})
-        if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "^(iOS|tvOS)$")
+        if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "^(iOS|tvOS|visionOS)$")
             find_library(COREFOUNDATION_FRAMEWORK NAMES CoreFoundation)
             if(COREFOUNDATION_FRAMEWORK)
                 set(EXTRA_LIBS -Wl,-framework,CoreFoundation ${EXTRA_LIBS})
diff --git a/alc/backends/coreaudio.cpp b/alc/backends/coreaudio.cpp
index 138859c..d835fc9 100644
--- a/alc/backends/coreaudio.cpp
+++ b/alc/backends/coreaudio.cpp
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 #include <AudioUnit/AudioUnit.h>
 #include <AudioToolbox/AudioToolbox.h>
 
-#if TARGET_OS_IOS || TARGET_OS_TV
+#if TARGET_OS_IOS || TARGET_OS_TV || TARGET_OS_VISION
 #define CAN_ENUMERATE 0
 #else
 #include <IOKit/audio/IOAudioTypes.h>
